        <div style="margin-top:17pt; text-align:center; width:456pt; line-height:12pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.25pt;">&#160;</font>
          <br >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:6pt;margin-left:69.66pt;width:456pt;">
        <div style="width:456pt; line-height:13pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.25pt;">D. Exchange rates and linkage base:</font><font style="font-weight:normal;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:13pt;">
          <font style="font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.25pt;">(1)</font><font style="letter-spacing:0.25pt;"> The financial statements of each of the Group&#8217;s subsidiaries were prepared in the currency of the main economic environment in which it operates (hereinafter: the &#8220;Functional Currency&#8221;). For the purpose of consolidating the financial statements, results and financial position of each of the Group&#8217;s member companies are translated into the NIS, which is the Company&#8217;s functional currency. The Group&#8217;s consolidated financial statements are presented in USD. For details regarding the exchange rates, and changes thereto, during the presented periods, see section (3).</font><font style="font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:13pt;">
          <font style="font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.25pt;">(2)</font><font style="letter-spacing:0.25pt;"> Balances linked to the consumer price index in Israel (hereinafter: the &#8220;CPI&#8221;) are presented according to the last known index on the balance sheet date (known CPI), or according to the index with respect to the last month of the reporting period (CPI in lieu), in accordance with the terms of the transaction.</font><font style="font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:8pt; width:456pt; line-height:13pt;font-weight:bold;">
          <font style="letter-spacing:0.25pt;">(3) Presented below are data regarding the exchange rates and CPI:</font><font style="font-weight:normal;font-family:Times New Roman, Times, serif ;letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </font>
